From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:09:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d-mtl: handlers tied to their objects, pools in the VM,
 paced presents

The M2a review's findings on the winemetal facade:
- A presented handler added after presentDrawable goes with the
  presenting command buffer (pending while uncommitted, else its queue's
  retirement thread): mtld3d adds its cadence and pacing handlers after
  presenting, and every vsync'd present waited out the 1 s cap.
- A command buffer or drawable whose last facade reference goes with
  handlers pending runs them then; its side tables go with it (test
  statuses, MetalFX textures, a queue's retirement thread); an entry
  made for an object the facade held nothing of starts afresh when a
  new object takes the address.
- autoreleasepool is winemetal's pool on every target (in the VM an
  autoreleased return with no pool open lived until the process ended),
  and the retirement thread drains one per buffer.
- waitUntilCompleted returns once the buffer's handlers have run, as
  Metal's does; commits and retirement keep one order.
- GPU start and end times are the GPU's (properties 2 and 3), a
  dispatch with another threadgroup size gets a pipeline node of its
  own, slot 27 is named and checked, an error's code is a hash of its
  description, and the page allocator is asked at the first page.
Tests: a handler run by a dropped buffer and by no later one, wait
after handlers, a default sampler's normalized coordinates, and in the
guest a pool that drains.

